# Claude auth — pick ONE of the two blocks below.

# (a) Subscription. Get a token with `claude setup-token`.
#     Add the ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL line only if you want LLM traffic to go through
#     the gateway (observability); leave it out to go direct to Anthropic.
#     Do NOT set ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN here — it would shadow the OAuth token.
CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN=
# ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL=http://host.boxlite.internal:3001/claude

# (b) API key. Setting ANY ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL — this gateway or an unrelated
#     proxy you already use — tells the box the credential lives outside it:
#     ANTHROPIC_API_KEY then stops being forwarded and stays on the host.
#     ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN becomes required instead, but its value is never
#     checked. Only omit ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL entirely if you want the key sent
#     into the box directly.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL=http://host.boxlite.internal:3001/api
# ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN=unused

# Optional — only needed if ANTHROPIC_API_KEY is not an Anthropic key (e.g. a
# LiteLLM key). Bare host only, no scheme and no path (e.g.
# litellm.example.net, not https://litellm.example.net/v1). Defaults to
# api.anthropic.com when unset. This is the gateway's *outbound* target for
# the /api route — distinct from ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL above, which is where the
# box sends traffic (the gateway itself). Setting this to the gateway's own
# address would not make sense and is not what it's for.
# ANTHROPIC_UPSTREAM_HOST=

# ANTHROPIC_MODEL=         # optional

# GitHub (optional) — enables gh + git push/pull over HTTPS
# GH_TOKEN=

# Git identity (optional)
# GIT_AUTHOR_NAME=
# GIT_AUTHOR_EMAIL=
